  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/mlidbom/Compze",
  "published": "2026-11-27T00:38:51.147Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- **`IProcessSemaphore` and `IProcessSemaphoreHold` are gone.** The semaphore came in 0.9.0-alpha for the one program that used it, whose first real load found a flaw within the day: a take waited behind takes that were only finishing. Compze.Threading.Interprocess holds only synchronization primitives that are well thought out, stable and tested for every consumer, so that program now has a semaphore of its own, built on `IProcessLock` and `IInterprocessObject<T>`. To upgrade, build what you need on those two, as it did, or keep to 0.9.0-alpha or 0.10.0-alpha.",
